Hi,

I'm working with various Gumstix Overo boards (OMAP 35XX) and found that
kernel versions from the linux-omap tree newer than 2.6.36 fail to boot
on the Overo, as in no output after "Uncompressing Linux... done,
booting the kernel." See attached for the complete serial console output
(latest 3.3 git version as of this writing, using omap2plus_defconfig).

I tried a git bisect between tags v2.6.36 and v2.6.37 with the following
results: After a few steps I hit versions that would fail to compile. If
I assume them to be good until getting a compilable commit again, the
bisect points at

commit 7b6181e06841f5ad15c4ff708b967b4db65a64de
Merge: 72e5806 bc487fb
Author: Linus Torvalds <torvalds@linux-foundation.org>
Date:   Mon Oct 25 13:46:56 2010 -0700

    Merge branch 'omap-for-linus' of
git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/tmlind/linux-omap-2.6

as the first faulty commit. If I mark non-compiling commits as bad,
bisect points at

commit bc487fb341af05120bccb9f59ce76302391dcc77
Author: Anand Gadiyar <gadiyar@ti.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 22 11:15:16 2010 -0700

    omap: complete removal of machine_desc.io_pg_offst and .phys_io

The first variant hits compilable and working commits before the fault,
so I assume 7b6181e06841f5ad15c4ff708b967b4db65a64de is the correct
result, but I couldn't find the actual problem.
config-2.6.36-05458-g7b6181e contains the configuration.

Compiler information (from Emdebian repository):
arm-linux-gnueabi-gcc (Ubuntu/Linaro 4.5.2-8ubuntu3) 4.5.2
Copyright (C) 2010 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
This is free software; see the source for copying conditions.  There is NO
warranty; not even for MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.

Any advice on how to solve this problem would be appreciated. If you
need additional information, please ask.

Kind regards,
Thomas Klute

